From 52b33d994c028aafbca36fdcf8e79293f9842b3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theodotdot <59372255+theodotdot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:02:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] feat: draw and hit-test above-lock layer surfaces over
 the session lock

While the session is locked, niri renders only the lock surface and routes
input only to it, so a layer-shell on-screen keyboard is neither visible nor
clickable. On a handheld without a hardware keyboard that leaves the session
impossible to unlock.

Add a layer rule, above-lock true: matched surfaces are drawn over the lock
surface and take pointer/touch input before it. It is opt-in and off by
default, so nothing changes without a config asking for it; layer-shell
popups of such surfaces are not drawn above the lock screen.
