+#### `above-lock`
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Set to `true` to keep the surface drawn *over* the session lock screen, and to keep it receiving pointer and touch input there.
+
+This exists for on-screen keyboards: without it, nothing but the lock screen itself is visible or clickable while the session is locked, so a device with no hardware keyboard cannot be unlocked.
+The surface is drawn above the lock surface regardless of the layer it asked for.
+
+Only layer surfaces matched by a rule with `above-lock true` are drawn and hit-tested over the lock screen; every other surface, including layer-shell popups, stays hidden.
+Anything drawn over a lock screen can imitate a password prompt, so only trusted clients (in practice: the keyboard) should be given this.
+
+```kdl
+// Keep the on-screen keyboard usable while the session is locked.
+layer-rule {
+    match namespace="^plasma-keyboard$"
+
+    above-lock true
+}
+```
+
 #### `baba-is-float`
 
 <sup>Since: 25.05</sup>
